    "plain_text": "Adolph Mollenhauer Dick was an heir from a New York family whose fortune combined sugar refining and banking. Educated at Yale, he inherited interests through both the Dick and Mollenhauer families and maintained the family’s Long Island estate. His life centred on private stewardship of inherited assets rather than a prominent independent operating career.",
